==Trivia==
*[[The Devil's Rhythm (Merciless)|The Devil's Rhythm]]'s English localization is inconsistent with [[Aku's Melody (Merciless)|Aku's Melody]]. Aku's Melody's Japanese name is Akuma no Senritsu (悪魔の旋律, "Devil's Melody"), and became Aku's Melody because Akuma (悪魔, "Devil") is the Japanese name of the [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] trait; as such, The Devil's Rhythm's Japanese name, Akuma no Ritsudō (悪魔の律動, "Devil's Rhythm"), would logically become "Aku's Rhythm", but 悪魔 was instead translated as "The Devil".
*[[Symphony of Bankruptcy (Merciless)|Symphony of Bankruptcy]]'s Japanese name, Dai Go-ban Hatan-chō (第五番破綻調, "No. 5 in Bankruptcy Key"), sounds the same as the Japanese translation of [[wikipedia:Symphony No. 5 (Beethoven)|No. 5 in C Minor]] (第5番 ハ短調) by [[wikipedia:Beethoven|Beethoven]]. The joke is that 破綻調 ("Bankruptcy Key") and ハ短調 ("C minor key") are both pronounced ''hatan-chō''.
**Although 破綻 was officially translated as "Bankruptcy", it can also mean "ruination" or "failure", referencing how [[Possessed Empress]] leads the Cat Empire to utter calamity.

